// FAQ data
const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What is the best web hosting for WordPress?',
    answer: '<p><strong>WP Engine</strong> is our top recommendation for WordPress hosting. It\'s specifically optimized for WordPress with automatic updates, staging environments, daily backups, and expert WordPress support. Sites hosted on WP Engine are noticeably faster and more secure than standard shared hosting.</p><p>For budget-conscious users, <strong>SiteGround</strong> offers excellent WordPress hosting starting at $2.99/month with solid performance and free SSL certificates.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'Shared hosting vs managed hosting: What\'s the difference?',
    answer: '<p><strong>Shared hosting</strong> puts multiple websites on one server, sharing resources. It\'s cheap ($2-10/month) but performance suffers when neighbors have traffic spikes. You manage everything yourself.</p><p><strong>Managed hosting</strong> handles server management, security, updates, and optimization for you. It costs more ($15-50/month) but saves hours of technical work and typically delivers better performance and security.</p><p>For serious businesses, managed hosting is worth the premium. For hobby sites or testing, shared hosting is fine.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'How much does web hosting cost?',
    answer: '<p>Web hosting costs range widely based on type and features:</p><ul><li><strong>Shared hosting:</strong> $2-15/month</li><li><strong>Managed WordPress:</strong> $15-50/month</li><li><strong>VPS hosting:</strong> $10-100/month</li><li><strong>Dedicated servers:</strong> $100-500+/month</li><li><strong>Cloud hosting:</strong> Pay-as-you-go, typically $10-100/month</li></ul><p>Most remote businesses do well with managed WordPress hosting in the $20-35/month range. Don\'t let cheap hosting cost you customers through slow load times.</p>'
