    question: 'What uptime should I expect from my host?',
    answer: '<p>Reputable hosts guarantee <strong>99.9% uptime</strong> or higher. Here\'s what that means in downtime:</p><ul><li>99.9% = 8.76 hours/year</li><li>99.95% = 4.38 hours/year</li><li>99.99% = 52.6 minutes/year</li></ul><p>Premium hosts like WP Engine, Kinsta, and Cloudways consistently deliver 99.99%+. Budget hosts typically hit 99.9% but may have occasional longer outages.</p><p>For business sites, prioritize hosts with strong uptime track records and SLA guarantees with credits for downtime.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I switch hosts without losing my website?',
    answer: '<p><strong>Yes, and most good hosts make it easy.</strong> The migration process typically involves:</p><ol><li>Signing up with new host</li><li>Migrating files and database (often done free by new host)</li><li>Testing on temporary URL</li><li>Updating DNS to point to new server</li><li>SSL certificate installation</li></ol><p>Most managed hosts offer <strong>free migration</strong> handled by their team. WP Engine, SiteGround, Kinsta, and Cloudways all migrate sites for free. The process typically takes 24-48 hours with minimal downtime.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'What is CDN and do I need one?',
    answer: '<p>A <strong>CDN (Content Delivery Network)</strong> stores copies of your website on servers worldwide. When someone visits your site, they load it from the nearest server, reducing load times significantly.</p><p>You need a CDN if:</p><ul><li>Your audience is geographically distributed</li><li>You have image-heavy content</li><li>Speed is a priority (it should be)</li></ul><p>Most managed hosts include CDN. WP Engine includes their Global Edge Security, Kinsta includes Cloudflare CDN, and Cloudways offers Cloudflare integration. For shared hosts, you can add Cloudflare\'s free tier yourself.</p>'
  },
