  <!-- Migration Guide -->
  <h2 id="migration-guide">Migrating to a New Host</h2>
  <p>
    Switching hosts is easier than you might think. Here's the process:
  </p>

  <h3>Step 1: Sign Up with New Host</h3>
  <p>
    Create your account with the new host. Don't cancel your old hosting yet—you'll run both briefly during transition.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 2: Request Migration</h3>
  <p>
    Most quality hosts offer free migration. WP Engine, SiteGround, Kinsta, and Cloudways all migrate sites for free.
    Provide your old host login details and they handle the technical work.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 3: Test on New Server</h3>
  <p>
    Your new host provides a temporary URL to test your site before going live. Check all pages, forms, and
    functionality. Fix any issues before switching DNS.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 4: Update DNS</h3>
  <p>
    Point your domain to the new server by updating DNS records. Your host provides the correct values. DNS propagation
    takes 24-48 hours—some visitors will see the old site during this window.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 5: Verify and Cancel Old Host</h3>
  <p>
    Once DNS has propagated and everything works, you can cancel your old hosting. Keep backups of the old site just in
    case.
  </p>

